        <mxCell id="NOTES" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;fillColor=#FFFDE7;strokeColor=#333333;" value="UGR evaluation rig — wiring (power, logic, motor, USB) · from CONNECTIONS.md Rev 2&lt;br&gt;• Pi → board: 40-way IDC ribbon into 2×20 header J2; 9 cores used.&lt;br&gt;• TMC2209 pins grouped by function, not physical order; check PDN_UART position on the silkscreen. MS1/MS2 are UART address straps: U1 MS1=GND MS2=GND (addr 0), U2 MS1=3V3 MS2=GND (addr 1).&lt;br&gt;• GROUND 1 = CH1 0 V at the star point; GROUND 2 = CH2 0 V / Pi GND. Joined only by the J2-6 wire; the camera tether GND is a second, unavoidable path.&lt;br&gt;• Rocker drawn as 3-terminal illuminated type (lamp to 0 V). XH pin order 1-4 = A+, A−, B+, B−.&lt;br&gt;• Fiducial LED not drawn (power source not defined)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="640" x="40" y="590" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
